  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Motor vehicle fuel sales, <span class="refper">2025</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/261002/dq261002a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/261002/dq261002a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-10-02T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The demand for motor vehicle fuels in Canada continued to grow in 2025, with gross sales of gasoline edging up 2.3% year over year to 44.8&#160;billion&#160;litres, a six-year high. Both gross and net sales of gasoline edged closer to levels seen before the COVID-19 pandemic. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
