      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Real gross domestic product was essentially unchanged in July, following three consecutive months of expansion.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Study: Taking the pulse: Perceptions of democracy in Canada</div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260929/dq260929b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260929/dq260929b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-29T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In spring&#160;2024, most Canadians aged 15&#160;years and older reported feeling at least a little or somewhat hopeful about the way democracy works in Canada. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Energy statistics, <span class="refper">July 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260929/dq260929c-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260929/dq260929c-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-29T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Primary energy production rose 2.7% year over year to 2.1&#160;million gigajoules in July, with five of six&#160;subsectors contributing to the increase.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Film and video distribution, <span class="refper">2025</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260929/dq260929d-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260929/dq260929d-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-29T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Following a strong rebound from the COVID-19&#160;pandemic in 2023, the film and video distribution industry saw continued growth in 2025, with operating revenues increasing by $154.3&#160;million (+9.0%) from 2023 to $1.9&#160;billion in 2025. While operating revenues have continued to recover since the pandemic, they were 1.1%&#160;below the pre-pandemic levels seen in 2019, as ongoing structural changes in content consumption and traditional film and video distribution channels have continued to reshape the industry. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
