  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Transportation and Supply Chain Indexes: announcement</div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260928/dq260928f-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260928/dq260928f-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-28T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Today, Statistics Canada announces the creation of the Transportation Services Index and the Supply Chain Services Prices Index. These indices were developed to measure changes in volumes and prices across transportation sectors using a methodology developed internally by Statistics Canada. The indices will be published for the first time on October&#160;19,&#160;2026. These data support analysis of economic activities, price movements and inflation dynamics.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">National tourism indicators, <span class="refper">second quarter 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260925/dq260925a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260925/dq260925a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-25T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Real tourism gross domestic product (GDP) grew 0.4% in the second quarter of 2026, following a 0.5% increase in the first quarter. In the second quarter, 1.77% of nominal GDP was attributable to tourism.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Government finance statistics, <span class="refper">second quarter 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260925/dq260925b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260925/dq260925b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-25T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In the second quarter, the Canadian general government recorded a surplus of $10.5&#160;billion, an increase of $2.3&#160;billion compared with the same quarter a year earlier. However, if social security funds are excluded, the general government recorded a deficit of $17.2&#160;billion. The federal government deficit ($4.1&#160;billion) increased by $1.1&#160;billion compared with the second quarter of 2025, as growth in expenses outpaced revenue, while the deficit of provincial and territorial governments ($10.1&#160;billion) increased by $0.3&#160;billion. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Screened passenger traffic at Canadian airports, <span class="refper">August 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260925/dq260925c-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260925/dq260925c-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-25T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In August, 6.1 million passengers passed through pre-board security screening at checkpoints operated at Canada's eight largest airports, up 6.1% from August 2025.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Natural resource indicators, <span class="refper">second quarter 2026</span></div>
