    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260925/dq260925d-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-25T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Data for the second quarter of 2026 for the Natural Resource Indicators (NRI) are now available, along with revised data for the first quarter of 2026.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Oilseed crushing statistics, <span class="refper">August 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260925/dq260925e-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260925/dq260925e-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-25T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Oilseed processors crushed 1.2&#160;million&#160;tonnes of canola in August, down 6.4% from July&#160;2026 and up 42.5% from August&#160;2025. Oil production reached 530.7&#160;thousand&#160;tonnes in August&#160;2026, while meal production was 724.9&#160;thousand&#160;tonnes.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Wholesale trade: Advance indicator, <span class="refper">August 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260925/dq260925f-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260925/dq260925f-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-25T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Statistics Canada is providing an advance estimate of sales in the wholesale trade sector. The advance results for August indicate that wholesale sales (excluding petroleum, petroleum products, and other hydrocarbons and excluding oilseed and grain) decreased 1.5%. The decline mainly reflects lower sales in the agricultural supplies industry group within the miscellaneous subsector and the motor vehicle and motor vehicle parts and accessories subsector. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Retail trade, <span class="refper">July 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260924/dq260924a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260924/dq260924a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-24T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Retail sales decreased 0.7% to $73.7&#160;billion in July. Sales were down in eight&#160;of nine&#160;subsectors, led by declines at general merchandise retailers.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Payroll employment, earnings and hours, and job vacancies, <span class="refper">July 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260924/dq260924b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260924/dq260924b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-24T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The number of employees receiving pay and benefits from their employer&#8212;measured as "payroll employment" in the Survey of Employment, Payrolls and Hours&#8212;was up by 26,100 (+0.1%) in July, following three consecutive increases from March to June, totalling 124,200 (+0.7%). On a year-over-year basis, payroll employment was up 171,900 (+0.9%) in July.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Aircraft movement and civil aviation statistics, <span class="refper">July 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260924/dq260924c-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260924/dq260924c-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-24T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Major Canadian airlines flew 8.4&#160;million passengers on scheduled and charter services in July, up 1.1% from July&#160;2025.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Open Database of Sports and Recreational Facilities, version 2.0</div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260924/dq260924d-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260924/dq260924d-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-24T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The Open Database of Sports and Recreational Facilities (ODSRF) (formerly known as the Open Database of Recreational and Sport Facilities) is a collection of open data containing the names, types and locations of sports and recreational facilities across Canada. The ODSRF includes open microdata from authoritative sources such as governments and professional associations. Data were collected from 2025 to 2026 and the ODSRF is provided as open data under the Open Government Licence - Canada.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Open Database of Healthcare Facilities, version 2.0</div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260924/dq260924e-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260924/dq260924e-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-24T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The Open Database of Healthcare Facilities (ODHF) is a collection of open data containing the names, types and locations of healthcare facilities across Canada. This dataset is a product of the Linkable Open Data Environment, an initiative to enhance the use and harmonization of open data from municipal, regional, provincial, territorial and federal sources.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Oil and gas extraction, <span class="refper">2025</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260924/dq260924f-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260924/dq260924f-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-24T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Data from the Oil and Gas Extraction Survey for 2025 are now available. The Oil and Gas Extraction Survey provides data on finances, income and balance sheets, as well as on operations of establishments in the oil and gas extraction industry.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Monthly Survey of Manufacturing: Advance indicator, <span class="refper">August 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260924/dq260924g-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260924/dq260924g-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-24T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Statistics Canada is providing an advance estimate of sales in the manufacturing sector. Advance results indicate that total manufacturing sales increased 1.1% in August. The largest increases were in the primary metal and chemical subsectors. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Canada's population estimates: Age and gender, <span class="refper">2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260923/dq260923a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260923/dq260923a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-23T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The population of Canada reached an estimated 41,798,407 people on July 1, 2026, an increase of 189,425 people (+0.5%) from July 1, 2025. This is the lowest annual July-to-July (or June to June before 1946) growth in the total size of the population since 1944/1945 (+126,000; +1.0%) and the lowest growth in percentage since 1915/1916 (+20,000; +0.3%). </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Canada's population estimates, <span class="refper">second quarter 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260923/dq260923b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260923/dq260923b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-23T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Population estimates for Canada, the provinces, and territories on July 1, 2026, are now available. These new data allow for an analysis of population change during the second quarter of 2026.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Economic and Social Reports, <span class="refper">September 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260923/dq260923c-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260923/dq260923c-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-23T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">There are four&#160;new articles in today's release of Economic and Social Reports.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Births, <span class="refper">2025</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260923/dq260923d-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260923/dq260923d-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-23T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">There were 372,521&#160;babies born in Canada in 2025, a 1.6% increase compared with&#160;2024. Similar to previous years, the proportion of boys (51.3%) was slightly higher than the proportion of girls (48.7%).</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Fertility and baby names, <span class="refper">2025</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260923/dq260923e-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260923/dq260923e-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-23T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In 2025, Canada's total fertility rate (TFR) was unchanged at 1.26 children per woman. It was identical to the all-time low observed in 2024.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Natural gas supply and disposition, <span class="refper">July 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260923/dq260923f-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260923/dq260923f-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-23T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">July data on natural gas transmission, storage and distribution are now available. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Refined petroleum products, <span class="refper">August 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260923/dq260923g-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260923/dq260923g-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-23T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Data for August on the production and inventories of refined petroleum products in Canada are now available upon request. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Travel between Canada and other countries, <span class="refper">July 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260922/dq260922a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260922/dq260922a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-22T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In July, the number of Canadian-resident return trips from the United States increased 10.1% year over year, while trips to Canada by United States residents rose 9.1%.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Opioid and stimulant consumption patterns in select Canadian cities, <span class="refper">January 2024 to March 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260922/dq260922b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260922/dq260922b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-22T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">New Canadian Wastewater Survey results from January 2024 to March 2026 show declining fentanyl levels in Metro Vancouver and relatively high stimulant consumption (e.g., methamphetamine and cocaine) in multiple cities in the Prairie provinces and in Moncton.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Vehicle registrations, <span class="refper">2025</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260922/dq260922c-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260922/dq260922c-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-22T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In 2025, a total of 27.6&#160;million road motor vehicles were registered in Canada, up 3.1% from the previous year. More than 9&#160;in 10&#160;vehicles (91.7%) were light-duty vehicles (LDVs), and 6.5% of this share was electric vehicles (EVs). Among registered light-duty EVs, the United States was the leading country of assembly, accounting for 35.6%, followed by Japan (20.8%) and Canada (14.9%). China (3.6%) ranked seventh, and more than 9&#160;in 10&#160;China-assembled EVs were battery electric vehicles (BEVs).</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Quarterly civil aviation statistics, <span class="refper">fourth quarter 2025</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260922/dq260922d-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260922/dq260922d-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-22T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Operating revenue for the 23 largest Canadian air carriers totalled $9.0 billion in the fourth quarter, up 3.4% compared with the same quarter of 2024. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
