      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The Employment Insurance Beneficiaries in Rural and Small Town Canada: Interactive Dashboard has been updated with data and analysis for the July&#160;2026 reference period. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Housing affordability in Canada, <span class="refper">2024</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260921/dq260921a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260921/dq260921a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-21T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In 2024, 23.2% of Canadian households lived in housing unaffordable to them&#8212;defined as spending 30% or more of their income on shelter costs&#8212;up from 22.0% in 2022. Renters (33.7%) were more likely than owners (17.4%) to live in unaffordable housing. This gap has been stable since 2018, the first cycle of this survey. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Investment in building construction, <span class="refper">July 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260921/dq260921b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260921/dq260921b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-21T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The total value of investment in building construction increased $270.9&#160;million (+1.2%) to $23.6&#160;billion in July.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Study: An overview of the banking industry in Canada: Understanding income within the context of regulatory and resilience requirements, <span class="refper">2020 to 2025</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260921/dq260921c-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260921/dq260921c-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-21T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">A sound banking system is a key component of the Canadian economy, and banks are well positioned to manage risk. The study, "An overview of the banking industry in Canada: Understanding income within the context of regulatory and resilience requirements" examines factors driving the income of banks (see Note to readers) and regulatory compliance, while highlighting recent developments in the banking industry.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Urban public transit, <span class="refper">July 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260921/dq260921d-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260921/dq260921d-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-21T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In July, 122.5&#160;million passenger trips were taken on urban transit networks in Canada, representing a 1.6% decrease, or 2.0&#160;million fewer rides, from July&#160;2025.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
