  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Canada's international transactions in securities, <span class="refper">July 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260917/dq260917a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260917/dq260917a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-17T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Canadian investors reduced their exposure to foreign securities by $30.6&#160;billion in July, led by sales of United States shares. Meanwhile, foreign investors added $20.7&#160;billion of Canadian securities to their holdings, led by a significant investment in federal government bonds. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Industrial product and raw materials price indexes, <span class="refper">August 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260917/dq260917b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260917/dq260917b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-17T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The Industrial Product Price Index rose 1.3% month over month in August and increased 13.5% year over year. Meanwhile, the Raw Materials Price Index rose 3.1% month over month and increased 22.8% year over year. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
