  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Building permits, <span class="refper">July 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260916/dq260916a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260916/dq260916a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-16T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In July, the total value of building permits issued in Canada declined $2.6&#160;billion (-17.3%) to reach $12.2&#160;billion.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Model-based principal field crop estimates, <span class="refper">August 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260916/dq260916b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260916/dq260916b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-16T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In 2026, Canadian farmers are projected to produce more corn for grain and soybeans but less wheat, canola, barley and oats, compared with 2025, according to recent yield model estimates using satellite imagery and agroclimatic data. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Health Reports, <span class="refper">September 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260916/dq260916c-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260916/dq260916c-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-16T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The health benefits of moderate-to-vigorous physical activity and the health risks of sedentary time are well known. Less is known about the health effects of light-intensity physical activity, the activity accumulated between sedentary and moderate, such as slow walking, household chores or light gardening.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
