  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Job vacancies, <span class="refper">second quarter 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260915/dq260915a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260915/dq260915a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-15T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Job vacancies held steady at 510,200 in the second quarter, following an increase of 13,300 (+2.7%) in the previous quarter. Job vacancies increased by 3,600 (+2.8%) for part-time jobs but were little changed for full-time jobs, and for permanent and temporary positions.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Wholesale trade, <span class="refper">July 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260915/dq260915b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260915/dq260915b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-15T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Wholesale sales (excluding petroleum, petroleum products, and other hydrocarbons and excluding oilseed and grain) increased&#160;0.3% in July. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">New motor vehicle sales, <span class="refper">July 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260915/dq260915c-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260915/dq260915c-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-15T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">There were 176,156&#160;new motor vehicles sold in Canada in July, a decrease of 2.0% from the same month one year earlier. However, sales in dollar terms increased 1.6% relative to July&#160;2025. Over the same period, the number of new passenger cars sold declined by 4.6%, while the number of new trucks sold declined 1.6%.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Consumer Price Index, <span class="refper">August 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260914/dq260914a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260914/dq260914a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-14T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The Consumer Price Index&#160;(CPI) rose 3.0% year over year in August, matching the 3.0% increase in July. On a seasonally adjusted monthly basis, the CPI increased 0.2% in August.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Monthly Survey of Manufacturing, <span class="refper">July 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260914/dq260914b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260914/dq260914b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-14T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Manufacturing sales declined 0.4% in July, mainly on decreased sales of chemicals and food product manufacturing. Meanwhile, sales in the petroleum and coal product subsector increased the most.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">National balance sheet and financial flow accounts, <span class="refper">second quarter 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260911/dq260911a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260911/dq260911a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-11T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The net worth of Canadian households&#8212;the value of all assets minus all liabilities&#8212;rose 2.9% in the second quarter of 2026 to eclipse $19 trillion, as a boon in equity markets translated into greater household net worth through higher asset valuations. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Leading indicator of international arrivals to Canada, <span class="refper">August 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260911/dq260911b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260911/dq260911b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-11T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In August, the preliminary number of international arrivals to Canada (Canadian-resident return trips, combined with US-resident and overseas-resident arrivals) by air and automobile totalled 6.9&#160;million, up 4.3% from the same month in 2025.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Canada's international investment position, <span class="refper">second quarter 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260910/dq260910a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260910/dq260910a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-09-10T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Canada's net foreign asset position, the difference between Canada's international financial assets and international liabilities, increased by $619.2 billion to reach $1,945.5 billion at the end of the second quarter. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
