    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Canada's current account balance (on a seasonally adjusted basis) went from a deficit of $8.3&#160;billion in the first quarter to a surplus of $8.8&#160;billion in the second quarter. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Payroll employment, earnings and hours, and job vacancies, <span class="refper">June 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260827/dq260827b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260827/dq260827b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-08-27T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The number of employees receiving pay and benefits from their employer&#8212;measured as "payroll employment" in the Survey of Employment, Payrolls and Hours&#8212;was little changed (+4,800;&#160;+0.0%) in June, following an increase of 45,000&#160;(+0.2%) in May. On a year-on-year basis, payroll employment was up by 155,000&#160;(+0.8%) in June.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Aircraft movement and civil aviation statistics, <span class="refper">June 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260827/dq260827c-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260827/dq260827c-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-08-27T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Major Canadian airlines flew 7.6&#160;million passengers on scheduled and charter services in June, edging up 0.5% from June&#160;2025.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
