  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Economic and Social Reports, <span class="refper">August 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260826/dq260826a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260826/dq260826a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-08-26T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">There are four&#160;new articles in today's release of Economic and Social Reports.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Canadian Housing Statistics Program, <span class="refper">2024</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260826/dq260826b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260826/dq260826b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-08-26T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In 2023, the median family income of first-time homebuyers was lower than that of repeat buyers in all jurisdictions for which data were available, except in British Columbia, where similar median incomes were reported for both groups.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Food services and drinking places, <span class="refper">June 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260826/dq260826c-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260826/dq260826c-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-08-26T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Total sales in the food services and drinking places subsector increased 0.5% in June to $8.8&#160;billion. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">National Travel Survey and Visitor Travel Survey, <span class="refper">first quarter 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260825/dq260825a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260825/dq260825a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-08-25T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">During the first quarter of 2026, Canadian residents took 78.7&#160;million trips within Canada and abroad, up 1.5% from the same quarter in 2025. From January to March&#160;2026, visitors from the United States and overseas countries took 4.5&#160;million trips to Canada, an increase of 3.5% compared with the first quarter of 2025.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Railway carloadings, <span class="refper">June 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260825/dq260825b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260825/dq260825b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-08-25T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In June, Canadian railways transported 30.9&#160;million tonnes of freight, up 3.2% from June one year earlier and the third consecutive monthly increase. Increased loadings of grains and other commodities more than offset steep declines in iron ores and coal. Higher volumes of freight traffic from US rail connections also contributed to the overall tonnage increase.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Wholesale trade: Advance indicator, <span class="refper">July 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260825/dq260825c-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260825/dq260825c-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-08-25T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Statistics Canada is providing an advance estimate of sales in the wholesale trade sector. The advance results for July indicate that wholesale sales (excluding petroleum, petroleum products, and other hydrocarbons and excluding oilseed and grain) decreased 0.6%. The decline mainly reflects lower sales in the agricultural supplies and mineral, ore and precious metal industry groups within the miscellaneous subsector. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Quarterly financial statistics for enterprises, <span class="refper">second quarter 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260824/dq260824a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260824/dq260824a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-08-24T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Operating profit reported by Canadian corporations rose to $228.2 billion in the second quarter, an increase of $20.1 billion (+9.7%) from the first quarter. The increase was mainly attributable to non-financial industries. Compared with the same quarter one year earlier, Canadian corporations' operating profit was up by $29.7 billion (+15.0%).</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Livestock estimates, <span class="refper">July 1, 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260824/dq260824b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260824/dq260824b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-08-24T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">On July&#160;1,&#160;2026, Canadian cattle, hog and sheep inventories were up compared with the same date one year earlier.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Natural gas supply and disposition, <span class="refper">June 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260824/dq260824c-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260824/dq260824c-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-08-24T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">June data on natural gas transmission, storage and distribution are now available. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Monthly Survey of Manufacturing: Advance indicator, <span class="refper">July 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260824/dq260824d-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260824/dq260824d-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-08-24T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Statistics Canada is providing an advance estimate of sales in the manufacturing sector. Advance results indicate that total manufacturing sales edged down 0.2% in July. The largest decreases were in the chemical and fabricated metal product subsectors. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Retail trade, <span class="refper">June 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260821/dq260821a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260821/dq260821a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-08-21T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Retail sales increased 0.6% to $74.3&#160;billion in June. Sales were up in seven&#160;of nine&#160;subsectors, led by increases at general merchandise retailers.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Quarterly civil aviation statistics, <span class="refper">third quarter 2025</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260821/dq260821b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260821/dq260821b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-08-21T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Operating revenue for the 23&#160;largest Canadian air carriers totalled $9.7&#160;billion in the third quarter of 2025, 0.7% higher compared with the same quarter in 2024. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Integrating the Canadian Health Measures Survey and administrative data for use in Statistics Canada's research data centres</div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260821/dq260821c-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260821/dq260821c-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-08-21T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Today, Statistics Canada is releasing new files that link the first seven&#160;cycles of the Canadian Health Measures Survey&#160;(CHMS), conducted from 2007 to 2009 (Cycle&#160;1) through 2022 to 2024 (Cycle&#160;7), with selected administrative databases. These linkage files enable researchers to follow the CHMS participants over time and examine how directly measured health characteristics are associated with health outcomes, including cancer incidence, hospitalization, emergency department use, mental health service use, survival and mortality.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
