    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The Consumer Price Index (CPI) rose 3.0% year over year in July, following a 2.8% gain in June. On a seasonally adjusted monthly basis, the CPI increased 0.3% in July.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Canada's international transactions in securities, <span class="refper">June 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260817/dq260817b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260817/dq260817b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-08-17T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Foreign investors added $40.8&#160;billion of Canadian securities to their holdings in June, mainly acquisitions of federal government debt securities and private corporate bonds. Meanwhile, Canadian investors acquired $35.4&#160;billion of foreign securities, primarily US corporate shares and bonds.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">New motor vehicle sales, <span class="refper">June 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260817/dq260817c-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260817/dq260817c-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-08-17T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In June, 190,167&#160;new motor vehicles were sold in Canada, an increase of 7.3% from the same month the previous year. In dollar terms, sales increased 9.1% in June compared with one year earlier. Over the same period, the number of new trucks sold rose by 8.0%, while the number of new passenger cars sold increased 2.9%.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
