      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Data on monthly average retail prices for selected products are now available for June. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Canadian international merchandise trade, <span class="refper">June 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260804/dq260804a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260804/dq260804a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-08-04T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In June, Canada's merchandise exports increased 0.4%, while imports edged up 0.2%. As a result, Canada's merchandise trade surplus with the world widened slightly from $3.7 billion in May to $3.9 billion in June.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Canadian international trade in services, <span class="refper">June 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260804/dq260804b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260804/dq260804b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-08-04T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Canada's international imports of services decreased 0.4% to $21.0&#160;billion in June, and its exports of services edged down 0.2% to $20.8&#160;billion. As a result, Canada's monthly international trade in services deficit remained essentially unchanged at $0.3&#160;billion in June. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
