    <updated>2026-07-28T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The Employment Insurance Beneficiaries in Rural and Small Town Canada: Interactive Dashboard has been updated with data and analysis for the May&#160;2026 reference period. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Railway carloadings, <span class="refper">May 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260727/dq260727a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260727/dq260727a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-07-27T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In May, Canadian railways carried 33.3&#160;million&#160;tonnes of freight, up slightly (+1.0%) from May&#160;2025. In May&#160;2026, higher shipments of grains and some energy products offset declines in coal and iron ores. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Industrial product and raw materials price indexes, <span class="refper">June 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260724/dq260724a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260724/dq260724a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-07-24T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The Industrial Product Price Index declined&#160;1.4% month over month in June and gained&#160;12.4% year over year. The Raw Materials Price Index decreased&#160;6.9% month over month in June and increased&#160;20.7% year over year. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Building construction price indexes, <span class="refper">second quarter 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260724/dq260724b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260724/dq260724b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-07-24T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Residential building construction costs increased 0.5% in the second quarter, following a 0.7% increase in the previous quarter. Non-residential building construction costs rose 1.4% in the second quarter, following a 0.9% increase in the previous quarter.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">New Housing Price Index, <span class="refper">June 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260724/dq260724c-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260724/dq260724c-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-07-24T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The New Housing Price Index (December&#160;2016=100) is now available for June. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Monthly Survey of Manufacturing: Advance indicator, <span class="refper">June 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260724/dq260724d-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260724/dq260724d-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-07-24T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Statistics Canada is providing an advance estimate of sales in the manufacturing sector. Advance results indicate that total manufacturing sales edged down 0.1% in June. The largest decrease was in the petroleum and coal product subsector. Excluding the petroleum and coal product subsector, total manufacturing sales rose 2.2% in June. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Wholesale trade: Advance indicator, <span class="refper">June 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260724/dq260724e-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260724/dq260724e-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-07-24T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Statistics Canada is providing an advance estimate of sales in the wholesale trade sector. The advance results for June indicate that wholesale sales (excluding petroleum, petroleum products, and other hydrocarbons and excluding oilseed and grain) increased&#160;2.7%. The increase mainly reflects higher sales in the machinery, equipment and supplies subsector.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Retail trade, <span class="refper">May 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260723/dq260723a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260723/dq260723a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-07-23T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Retail sales increased&#160;1.0% to $73.7&#160;billion in May. Sales were up in all nine&#160;subsectors, led by increases at gasoline stations and fuel vendors. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Travel between Canada and other countries, <span class="refper">May 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260723/dq260723b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260723/dq260723b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-07-23T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In May, the number of Canadian-resident return trips from the United States increased 9.9% year over year, while trips to Canada by US residents jumped by 13.0%. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Employment Insurance, <span class="refper">May 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260723/dq260723c-eng.htm"></link>
