    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Labour Force Survey, <span class="refper">June 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260710/dq260710a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260710/dq260710a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-07-10T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Employment was little changed in June (+18,000; +0.1%) and the employment rate rose 0.1 percentage points to 60.8%. The unemployment rate declined 0.1 percentage points to 6.5%.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Building permits, <span class="refper">May 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260710/dq260710b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260710/dq260710b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-07-10T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In May, the total value of building permits issued in Canada decreased $215.0&#160;million&#160;(-1.7%) to reach $12.4&#160;billion.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Farm product prices, <span class="refper">May 2026</span></div>
