  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Firearms and intimate partner violence in Canada</div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260708/dq260708a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260708/dq260708a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-07-08T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In 2024, there were 1,096 victims of police-reported firearm-related intimate partner violence in Canada, representing a rate of 3.1 victims per 100,000 population aged 12 years and older.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Study: Feeling the heat: More than half of Canadians are highly concerned about climate change</div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260708/dq260708b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260708/dq260708b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-07-08T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In 2025, over half&#160;(53%) of Canadians were "very" or "extremely" concerned about climate change, and almost one-third&#160;(30%) of Canadians felt stressed about climate change at least once a month. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Retail Commodity Survey, <span class="refper">April 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260708/dq260708c-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260708/dq260708c-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-07-08T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Retail sales reached $73.5 billion in April, an increase of 3.2% compared with the same month one year earlier. Higher sales were reported in 12 of the 18 commodity classes.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Nunavut Air Exit Survey and Nunavut Cruise Exit Survey, <span class="refper">third quarter 2025</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260708/dq260708d-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260708/dq260708d-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-07-08T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">During the third&#160;quarter of&#160;2025, non-Nunavut-resident visitors took 22,800&#160;trips to Nunavut, down&#160;8.8% from the third&#160;quarter of&#160;2024. Nonetheless, over the same period, total visitor spending in the territory increased&#160;4.5% to $46.1&#160;million. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Canadian international merchandise trade, <span class="refper">May 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260707/dq260707a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260707/dq260707a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-07-07T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In May, Canada's merchandise exports increased 0.9%, while imports edged down 0.2%. As a result, Canada's merchandise trade surplus with the world widened from $3.4 billion in April to $4.2 billion in May.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Study: Individual and institutional investors in residential real estate, <span class="refper">2022</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260707/dq260707b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260707/dq260707b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-07-07T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">In 2022, rental properties were largely owned by small-scale investors in five of the six Canadian provinces studied. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Canadian international trade in services, <span class="refper">May 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260707/dq260707c-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260707/dq260707c-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-07-07T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Canada's international imports of services increased&#160;2.0% to $21.2&#160;billion in May, and its exports of services increased&#160;0.9% to $20.8&#160;billion. As a result, Canada's monthly international trade in services deficit widened from $0.2&#160;billion in April to $0.5&#160;billion in May.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">National culture indicators, <span class="refper">fourth quarter 2025 and first quarter 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260707/dq260707d-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260707/dq260707d-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-07-07T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Real gross domestic product&#160;(GDP) for the culture and sport sectors in Canada grew by&#160;0.4% in the first quarter of&#160;2026, slightly slower than the 0.6%&#160;growth in the fourth quarter of&#160;2025. On a nominal basis, GDP for the culture and sport sectors increased&#160;0.9% in the first quarter of&#160;2026, following a 1.8%&#160;increase in the previous quarter.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Sawmills, <span class="refper">April 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260706/dq260706a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260706/dq260706a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-07-06T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Lumber production decreased 0.3% from March to 3&#160;861.4&#160;thousand cubic metres in April. Production was down 9.7% from April&#160;2025.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
