  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Foreign control in the Canadian economy, <span class="refper">2024</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260624/dq260624a-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260624/dq260624a-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-06-24T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">The foreign-controlled share of assets in Canada was 13.9% in 2024. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Economic and Social Reports, <span class="refper">June 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260624/dq260624b-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260624/dq260624b-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-06-24T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">There are four&#160;new articles in today's release of Economic and Social Reports.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Labour market outcomes for college and university graduates, <span class="refper">2010 to 2022</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260624/dq260624c-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260624/dq260624c-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-06-24T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Today, Statistics Canada is releasing data on labour market outcomes for college and university graduates for the graduating classes of 2010&#160;to&#160;2022. This release includes information on the median employment income by educational qualification, field of study, gender, age group and status of student in Canada. This information is available at the national, provincial and territorial levels. For the first time, this release also includes information on Canadian graduates by Indigenous identity and racialized group.</div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
  <entry>
    <title type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Monthly Survey of Manufacturing: Advance indicator, <span class="refper">May 2026</span></div>
    </title>
    <link href="https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260624/dq260624d-eng.htm"></link>
    <id>https://www.statcan.gc.ca/daily-quotidien/260624/dq260624d-eng.htm</id>
    <updated>2026-06-24T08:30:00-04:00</updated>
    <summary type="xhtml">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Statistics Canada is providing an advance estimate of sales in the manufacturing sector. Advance results indicate that total manufacturing sales increased 1.1% in May. The largest increases were in the motor vehicle industry group as well as the chemical subsector. </div>
    </summary>
  </entry>
</feed>